# bootstrap.conf — inputs for bootstrap.sh
#
# Copy to `bootstrap.conf` and edit. Nothing in bootstrap.sh is hardcoded; every
# value a repository could reasonably differ on lives here.
#
# This file is sourced by bash. Keep it to plain assignments.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- target ----

# Repository to configure, as OWNER/NAME. Leave empty to use the repository of
# the current directory.
REPO=""

# Account or organisation that will own the project board. Leave empty to use
# the repository owner.
PROJECT_OWNER=""

# Title of the board. Also the idempotency key: a board with this title on this
# owner is reused rather than duplicated.
PROJECT_TITLE="Delivery board"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- fields ----
#
# Three single-select fields, one job each (see 05-github-mechanics.md §5.1).
# One option per line. Blank lines and leading whitespace are ignored.

# Lane — which part of the code a ticket touches. Name these after PATHS, not
# features. One lane, one seat, always. The last option is the escape hatch for
# a filer who does not know; it must exist or people will guess.
LANES="
  interface
  service
  data
  platform
  shared — needs a senior call
"

# Owner — the seniority the work needs. Follows the files, not the difficulty.
OWNERS="
  senior
  junior
  unsure — needs a senior call
"

# Seat — the slot an agent occupies. Never the vendor name; which agent fills a
# slot is a per-checkout concern, not a board concern.
SEATS="
  SR1
  SR2
  JR1
  JR2
"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- labels ----
#
# One label per line, as: name|colour|description
# Colour is a six-digit hex with no leading '#'.
#
# Labels are for filtering the ISSUE LIST. They do not populate board fields —
# those are separate systems that happen to share a word (§5.2).

LABELS="
  lane: interface|1d76db|Touches presentation-layer paths
  lane: service|1d76db|Touches service-layer paths
  lane: data|1d76db|Touches storage and migration paths
  lane: platform|1d76db|Touches build, config and tooling paths
  lane: shared|b60205|Touches files no single lane owns — needs serialising
  owner: senior|5319e7|Work that needs the senior bar
  owner: junior|5319e7|Work inside a well-fenced lane
  blocked|d93f0b|Must not start yet — see the blocked-by dependency
  security|b60205|Touches money, auth, tenant isolation or a migration
"

# ------------------------------------------------------------ milestones ----
#
# One milestone per line, as: title|description
#
# Milestones are DISJOINT — an issue belongs to exactly one, so they cannot
# nest (§5.4). The release is the union of all of them closing, not a milestone
# of its own. A milestone must be able to END; a permanent area of the system is
# a Lane, not a milestone.

MILESTONES="
  Core capability|The one thing the product must do. Closes when the core path works end to end.
  Production safeguards|Security, observability, failure handling and cost controls.
  Launch blockers|Everything else that must be true before release. Not a dumping ground.
"
